    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d394">

                <pb facs="0556" n="450" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg450"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Denby to Mr. Blaine</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-09-26"><hi rendition="#italic">September 26,
                            1891</hi>.</date> (Received November 10.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1393.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose a copy of a
                    dispatch to me from Consul Andrews, giving a description of the riot at Ichang.
                    Mr. Sowerby, who was injured by the mob, proves to be an Englishman. It is
                    gratifying to know that amid all the trouble and danger of the past four months
                    no American has been injured.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Denby</hi>.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d394-a1.xml" xpointer="d394-a1"/>
            </div>
